What loneOpT Is

SEQ 327 R1 (Tony, 2026-10-09): a lone operator (+, !, * ...) is NOT an ExpressioN. The
candidate (switch on) refuses it BY NAME: REFUSED + -- a prefix operator with no operand
after it. pop.sh runs this fixture WITH THE SWITCH ON and pins one named refusal per
operator. Switch off the old road reads a verdict instead (orc_old's oldRoad column).
The refusal ends loSay, so no LO line prints for either; the sentinel says the run
reached its foot.
